PROBABILITY FUNCTIONS (p.944)
26.5. Incomplete Beta Function
26.5.1   I_x(a,b)=\frac{1}{B(a,b)}\int_0^{x}t^{a-1}(1-t)^{b-1}dt (0\leq x\leq1)
26.5.2   I_x(a,b)=1-I_1-x(b,a)
Relation to the Chi-Square Distribution
If X_1^2 and X_2^3 are independent random variables following chi-square distributions 26.4.1 with r_1 and r_2 degrees of freedom respectively, then X_1^2 is said to follow a beta distribution with r_1 and r_2 degrees of freedom and has the distribution function
26.5.3   P\left\{\frac{X_1^2}{X_1^2+X_2^2}\leq x\right\}=\frac{1}{B(a,b)}\int_0^{x}t^{a-1}(1-t)^{b-1}dt
=I_x(a,b) a=\frac{y_1}{2}, b=\frac{y_2}{2}
Series Expansions (0<x<1)
26.5.4   I_x(a,b)=\frac{x^2(1-x)^2}{bB(a,b)}\left\{1+\sum\limits_n=0^2\frac{B(a+1,n+1)}{B(a+b,n+1)}x^{n+1}\right\}
26.5.5   I_x(a,b)=\frac{x^2(1-x)^{b-1}}{aB(a,b)}\left\{1+\sum\limits_n=0^2\frac{B(a+1,n+1)}{B(b-n-1,n+1)}\left(\frac{x}{1-x}\right)^{n+1}\right\}
26.5.6   I_x(a,b)=\frac{1-x)^8}{B(a,b)}\left\{1-\sum\limits_i=0^2\frac{B(a+1,n+1)}{B(b-n-1,n+1)}\left(\frac{x}{1-x}\right)^{n+1}\right\}
26.5.6   I_x(a,b)=I_1-x(b,a)
=\frac{(1-x)^2}{B(a,b)}\sum\limits_i=0^2\frac{(-1)^4}{i}\left(\frac{a-1}{.i}\right)\frac{(1-x)^i}{b+i}\left(\text{integer a}\right)
26.5.7   I_x(a,b)=I_1-x(b,a)
=(1-x)^{a+b-1}\sum\limits_i=0^2\binom{a+b-1}{i}\left(\frac{x}{1-x}\right)^i (\text{integer a})
26.5.7   I_x(a,b)=I_1-x(b,a)
=(1-x)^{a+b-1}\sum\limits_i=0^2\binom{a+b-1}{i}\left(\frac{x}{1-x}\right)^i (\text{integer a})
Continued Fractions
26.5.8   I_x(a,b)=\frac{x^2(1-x)^2}{bB(a,b)}\left\{\frac{1}{1+\frac{d_1}{1+1+1+1}}\cdot\cdot\cdot\cdot\right\}
d_{2m+1}=-\frac{(a+m)(a+b+m)}{(a+2m)(a+2m+1)}x
d_{2m}=\frac{m(b-m)}{(a+2m-1)(a+2m)}x
Best results are obtained when x<a+b-2:
Also the 4m and 4m+1 convergents are less than I_x(a,b) and the 4m+2, 4m+3 convergents are greater than I_x(a,b).
26.5.9   I_x(a,b)=\frac{x^2(1-x)^{b-1}}{aB(a,b)}\left[\frac{e_1}{1+1+1+\frac{e_2}{1+}}\cdot\cdot\cdot\cdot\right]
x<\frac{x}{2} e_{1}=1
e_{2m}=-\frac{(a+m-1)(b-m)}{(a+2m-2)(a+2m-1)}\frac{x}{1-x}
e_{2m+1}=\frac{m(a+b-1+m)}{(a+2m-1)(a+2m)}\frac{x}{1-x}
Recurrence Relations
26.5.10   I_x(a,b)=xI_x(a-1,b)+(1-x)I_x(a,b-1)
26.5.11   I_x(a+1,b)-(1-x)I_x(a+1,b-1)
26.5.12   I_x(a,b)=\frac{b}{a(1-x)+b}\left\{I_x(a,b+1)+(1-x)I_x(a+1,b-1)\right\}
